EDIT the existing QdrantService ctor body (currently L64-66): REPLACE the line `_client = new QdrantClient(host, port: _options.GrpcPort);` (L66) with a comment + the M11a ctor:
  // [IMP:M11a][QdrantService][PROGRESS] ApiKey pass-through to QdrantClient — backward-compatible (apiKey defaults null)
  _client = new QdrantClient(host, port: _options.GrpcPort, apiKey: _options.ApiKey);
The named-parameter `apiKey:` SKIPS the `bool https = false` positional default (Qdrant.Client 1.18.1 ctor signature: QdrantClient(string host, int port = 6334, bool https = false, string? apiKey = null, TimeSpan grpcTimeout = default, ILoggerFactory? loggerFactory = null) — operator web-verified). STRICTLY LOCAL single-line edit + the [IMP:M11a] inline source comment above it. DO NOT touch: the EnsureCollectionExistsAsync method, the BuildFilter/BuildCompactFilter/CreatePayloadIndexIdempotentAsync helpers, the Upsert/Search/Count/Delete/Get/GetBatchForCompactAsync methods, the IQdrantService interface, the _client/_options/_logger fields, the Uri parsing + host extraction (L64-65 stay), the M5 BUG_FIX_CONTEXT scars (Distance.Dot/Datetime-range-index/PointStruct.Payload/BuildFilter-entryType/Direction.Asc — preserved verbatim). The MODULE_CONTRACT header [GREP_SUMMARY] + [CHANGES] are APPENDED additively (M5 entries preserved). NO new [IMP:N] runtime LDD marker — the [IMP:M11a] is an INLINE SOURCE COMMENT for @debug/@qa grep traceability, NOT an ILogger emission; LddMarkers.cs is NOT touched (no new constant). Backward-compatibility: apiKey: _options.ApiKey where _options.ApiKey is null → QdrantClient connects without auth (identical to M5 behavior) → the QdrantServiceIntegrationTests ctor L241 (new QdrantClient("localhost", port: 6334), no apiKey: arg) stays green against unauthenticated Docker qdrant/qdrant.
